                <pb facs="1537" n="1339" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1339"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">J. C. S.
                    Files</note>
                <head>No. 1286<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the United States Chiefs of
                        Staff</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        C. C. S. 889/3</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-21">21 July 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">British Participation in the
                            War Against Japan</hi></p>
                <p>General MacArthur and Admiral Nimitz welcome the visit of a British
                    corps commander and accompanying officers. General
                        MacArthur suggests that they should arrive at an early date, and
                    if practicable by 1 August.</p>
                <p>It is suggested that further matters connected with this visit be handled on an
                    operational basis between the British Joint Staff Mission and the operating
                    agencies concerned of the War and Navy
                    Departments</p>
            </div>
